Search
      Binary Search
              Divide the search space in half each step based on whether the midpoint is higher or lower than the target
              log N
              LC 34
              
      Rotated Search
              Locate which half of the array remains normally sorted, then use standard binary search boundaries on that side
              LC 33
      
      Matrix Search
              LC 240
      
      Answer space Search
              Guess a solution in a valid range [low, high], test its feasibility via a helper function, and shrink the range accordingly
              LC 410

Pointers
        Opposing Pointers (Greedy State)
              Move the pointer that currently bottlenecks the overall objective inward to search for a globally better configuration
              LC 11
              
        Opposing Pointers (Boundary State)
              Maintain running historical extremes (like max/min heights encountered so far) to calculate localized, 
              cumulative results at the smaller boundary's position.
              LC 42
              
        Fast and Slow Pointers
              Advance one pointer twice as fast as the other to detect cycles or pinpoint the exact middle of a structure
              LC 142
              
        Sliding Window
              Shift a window of static size $k$ across the data by adding the incoming element and dropping the outgoing one
              LC 438
              
        Dynamic Window
              Expand the window to find a valid state, then shrink it from the left to find the optimal/smallest valid subarray
              LC 76

Stack 
        Monotonic 
            Hold elements linearly on a stack to "wait" for their future answer, 
            bypassing a polynomial $O(n^2)$ look-forward scan for an $O(n)$ solution

            LC 84
